From: mscharged-port
Subject: Declare the DWC API with the SDK's 32-bit widths
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility

The game-facing DWC forward headers spell the SDK's u32 and s32 as
unsigned long and long, one width on the Wii. On a 64-bit host long has
eight bytes: the declarations no longer match the DWC definitions, and
DWC_GetLastErrorEx would store four bytes into the game's eight-byte
error code. The headers take the definitions' types, and NetworkSession
keeps its DWC error code and allocator callbacks at the same widths.

diff --git a/include/Game/NetworkSession.h b/include/Game/NetworkSession.h
index 64bc48a..8f0e01d 100644
--- a/include/Game/NetworkSession.h
+++ b/include/Game/NetworkSession.h
@@ -638,9 +638,9 @@ public:
     /* 0x247C */ int mGameNumber;
     /* 0x2480 */ int mOverlayRequest;
     /* 0x2484 */ int mPoppedOverlay;
-    long GetDWCErrorCode() const { return mDWCErrorCode; }
+    s32 GetDWCErrorCode() const { return mDWCErrorCode; }
 
-    /* 0x2488 */ long mDWCErrorCode;
+    /* 0x2488 */ s32 mDWCErrorCode;
     /* 0x248C */ DWCErrorType mDWCErrorType;
     /* 0x2490 */ int mDWCLastError;
     /* 0x2494 */ u8 mFriendsMatchProcessingSuspended;
